    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0915" n="721" xml:id="pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Rumania)/7–2645:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 820<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Representative in Rumania</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Melbourne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d820-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-26T10:00:00+02:00">July 26, 1945—10 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>504. Soviet officials of the Allied Control Commission on July 24 verbally stated
                    that the program providing for a revised operation of Allied Control Commission
                    as reported in General Schuyler’s
                        War
                    Dept telegram July 16 No M–1250<anchor n="2" xml:id="d820-f2"/> did not apply to this
                    mission (This is 504) with respect to permitting it to determine unilaterally
                    the number of its personnel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Melbourne</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d820-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d820-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this message was included in telegram No. 140 of July 27 from
                        Grew to Byrnes (file No. 800.00 Summaries/7–2745).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d820-f2" n="2" xml:id="d820-f2-content">
